1
00:00:53,011 --> 00:00:54,471
<i>Why did your father escape?</i>

2
00:00:54,554 --> 00:00:56,347
Mang Mario escaped?

3
00:00:57,640 --> 00:00:58,683
Mikoy, did you know about this?

4
00:01:43,978 --> 00:01:45,188
I'm not sure.

5
00:01:45,772 --> 00:01:47,982
You know how much they love explosions.

6
00:01:48,066 --> 00:01:50,568
Most of the time, literally.

7
00:01:52,821 --> 00:01:54,697
Do you think she's back?

8
00:01:54,781 --> 00:01:55,615
Huh?

9
00:01:57,325 --> 00:01:58,827
Did I hear that right?

10
00:01:59,828 --> 00:02:01,704
You met with Chiara.

11
00:02:01,788 --> 00:02:03,039
When? Where?

12
00:02:07,710 --> 00:02:11,714
I just didn't want you to worry anymore.

13
00:02:12,423 --> 00:02:14,425
I worry every day.

14
00:02:14,509 --> 00:02:16,469
Every single minute. You know that.

15
00:02:26,980 --> 00:02:28,982
It looks like the Pinagpalas

16
00:02:29,065 --> 00:02:31,401
are under police protection too.

17
00:02:33,570 --> 00:02:34,612
Well,

18
00:02:36,489 --> 00:02:37,574
at least then,

19
00:02:38,199 --> 00:02:41,119
even if Chiara is far away from us,

20
00:02:41,202 --> 00:02:42,579
she still has family with her.

21
00:02:42,662 --> 00:02:43,788
It’s just…

22
00:02:46,457 --> 00:02:48,626
La Morte Bianca is looking for them.

23
00:02:55,174 --> 00:02:57,427
- Should we go to her?
- We can't.

24
00:03:00,638 --> 00:03:02,891
The police still see us as the enemy.

25
00:03:04,434 --> 00:03:07,312
As long as the Moravianos
are part of the Concordat,

26
00:03:07,896 --> 00:03:09,814
all eyes will be on us.

27
00:03:10,523 --> 00:03:12,901
This is exactly what I feared.

28
00:03:12,984 --> 00:03:15,111
That one day we'd have to choose

29
00:03:15,653 --> 00:03:18,698
between the Concordat and Chiara.

30
00:03:26,205 --> 00:03:27,832
Stop it. He's just asking you.

31
00:03:27,916 --> 00:03:29,083
You're useless!

32
00:03:35,632 --> 00:03:37,217
Negative again.

33
00:04:05,411 --> 00:04:06,871
Well, as expected,

34
00:04:06,955 --> 00:04:09,749
Chiara got out of her handcuffs
within 24 hours.

35
00:04:09,832 --> 00:04:11,417
But other than that,

36
00:04:11,501 --> 00:04:13,169
she's very cooperative.

37
00:04:20,051 --> 00:04:22,178
Are they giving you a hard time?

38
00:04:27,850 --> 00:04:30,103
Come on, tell me.

39
00:04:30,186 --> 00:04:33,648
The sooner we know,
the sooner we can solve it.

40
00:04:36,442 --> 00:04:39,153
I don't think that even if I told you
the problem right away,

41
00:04:39,237 --> 00:04:41,155
we'd be able to solve it that quickly.

42
00:04:46,953 --> 00:04:48,454
Mr. Mario escaped.

43
00:04:48,538 --> 00:04:49,706
What?

44
00:04:49,789 --> 00:04:52,959
Mario escaped? When?

45
00:04:53,042 --> 00:04:55,295
Last night, before Chiara arrived.

46
00:04:55,378 --> 00:04:57,005
Where did he go?

47
00:04:57,880 --> 00:04:59,507
We don't know, sir.

48
00:05:02,635 --> 00:05:04,804
And sir, what complicates it even more,

49
00:05:05,388 --> 00:05:08,308
is that when we asked Mikoy and Mrs. Tess,

50
00:05:08,391 --> 00:05:09,350
they didn't know either.

51
00:05:10,977 --> 00:05:12,603
He only left a letter.

52
00:05:12,687 --> 00:05:13,896
<i>A letter?</i>

53
00:05:17,317 --> 00:05:20,028
when one of you reports to the office,

54
00:05:20,111 --> 00:05:21,946
bring that letter with you.

55
00:05:29,620 --> 00:05:30,455
Okay, sir.

56
00:05:39,338 --> 00:05:41,007
Sir, what is this?

57
00:05:41,758 --> 00:05:43,509
Where is this? What happened?

58
00:05:44,635 --> 00:05:47,513
<i>Those are photos of the recent destruction</i>

59
00:05:47,597 --> 00:05:49,891
in a fishing community.

60
00:05:50,391 --> 00:05:52,143
Barangay San Arsiso.

61
00:06:47,532 --> 00:06:48,491
That's horrible.

62
00:06:48,574 --> 00:06:51,327
They didn't even choose
their victims. Look, there are…

63
00:06:51,911 --> 00:06:53,913
children and elderly people.

64
00:06:53,996 --> 00:06:56,457
There are even people
with disabilities caught in it.

65
00:06:56,541 --> 00:06:57,416
<i>Chiara was right.</i>

66
00:07:07,093 --> 00:07:08,594
Isn't there anything we can do?

67
00:07:09,887 --> 00:07:12,181
under Philippine law, no.

68
00:07:15,893 --> 00:07:19,063
But here in the Philippines,
we can't even enforce

69
00:07:19,647 --> 00:07:21,607
our local laws.

70
00:07:31,909 --> 00:07:33,453
We can't just wait

71
00:07:33,536 --> 00:07:36,205
for the next island
they're going to attack

72
00:07:36,289 --> 00:07:37,373
and destroy.

73
00:07:41,836 --> 00:07:44,547
so there are over 7,000 possibilities.

74
00:08:34,347 --> 00:08:35,681
Really? Me?

75
00:08:36,516 --> 00:08:37,350
Wait, did you…

76
00:08:38,142 --> 00:08:40,186
run this by Agent Alex first?

77
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:46,859
We're dead.

78
00:08:48,861 --> 00:08:50,446
It's not just

79
00:08:50,530 --> 00:08:53,115
the information she has
about La Morte Bianca

80
00:08:53,199 --> 00:08:54,450
and the Concordat

81
00:08:54,534 --> 00:08:56,285
that she's offering us.

82
00:09:07,129 --> 00:09:10,424
You're such a beautiful girl,
yet you're so stubborn.

83
00:09:20,977 --> 00:09:21,936
It's just that…

84
00:09:22,019 --> 00:09:23,271
Obviously,

85
00:09:24,230 --> 00:09:28,109
I worked hard to earn
good standing in this safehouse.

86
00:09:28,192 --> 00:09:31,737
And all of that could go to waste

87
00:09:31,821 --> 00:09:34,156
because of what you're offering.

88
00:09:41,289 --> 00:09:44,625
Sooner or later,
La Morte Bianca will find us.

89
00:10:01,309 --> 00:10:04,812
There is a budget allocated to us
by the Presidential Office.

90
00:10:04,895 --> 00:10:06,147
The problem is,

91
00:10:06,230 --> 00:10:08,149
it's difficult to access.

92
00:10:13,070 --> 00:10:16,532
So we have an additional budget,
but we can't access it?

93
00:10:16,616 --> 00:10:18,200
What's going on?

94
00:10:18,284 --> 00:10:21,245
Wait. Why me?

95
00:10:21,746 --> 00:10:23,414
Why are you asking me?

96
00:10:27,627 --> 00:10:31,589
One, you're not affiliated
with the Moravianos.

97
00:10:31,672 --> 00:10:34,592
So you're not on La Morte Bianca's radar.

98
00:10:42,767 --> 00:10:45,770
The agency isn't keeping
a close eye on you.

99
00:10:47,772 --> 00:10:49,523
I'm just thinking,

100
00:10:49,607 --> 00:10:52,610
if we end up teaming up with Chiara

101
00:10:52,693 --> 00:10:54,987
and build a team around her,

102
00:10:55,529 --> 00:10:58,324
wouldn't that be a bit
tricky and dangerous?

103
00:10:58,407 --> 00:11:00,993
Because we won't just be
dealing with the Moravianos,

104
00:11:01,077 --> 00:11:02,203
but the Concordat as well.

105
00:11:03,204 --> 00:11:04,538
But haven't we

106
00:11:05,289 --> 00:11:07,291
overcome our oppressors before?

107
00:11:07,375 --> 00:11:09,502
The ones who colonized us.

108
00:11:15,174 --> 00:11:16,300
That in this day and age,

109
00:11:16,926 --> 00:11:19,845
we're the ones who need
to stand up for our country?

110
00:11:24,600 --> 00:11:25,935
<i>We will not be oppressed.</i>

111
00:11:26,769 --> 00:11:29,855
So you're really going through
with your plan?

112
00:11:35,277 --> 00:11:36,821
Lastly,

113
00:11:36,904 --> 00:11:40,616
I think you're the perfect fit
for this task

114
00:11:40,699 --> 00:11:42,201
because I believe

115
00:11:42,284 --> 00:11:44,120
I can count on you.

116
00:12:02,513 --> 00:12:04,723
Sir, I don't want to rush this decision.

117
00:12:07,601 --> 00:12:10,855
But because Chiara Valtrovi is involved,

118
00:12:10,938 --> 00:12:13,149
I can't bring myself
to trust her just yet.

119
00:12:14,275 --> 00:12:15,693
So my question is,

120
00:12:16,360 --> 00:12:18,946
how exactly will we launch this plan?

121
00:12:29,623 --> 00:12:32,501
Cocoy, what I'm asking you to do
isn't illegal.

122
00:12:35,129 --> 00:12:39,091
It just doesn't have
the agency's permission.

123
00:12:40,176 --> 00:12:43,095
But technically speaking,
you're still in the clear.

124
00:12:44,889 --> 00:12:46,557
And most importantly,

125
00:12:47,057 --> 00:12:48,809
the offer is substantial.

126
00:13:20,257 --> 00:13:22,927
I didn't know you were nocturnal.

127
00:13:25,137 --> 00:13:26,222
I'm just used to it.

128
00:13:27,348 --> 00:13:29,600
My senses are sharper at night.

129
00:13:30,684 --> 00:13:34,939
So tell me,
what's with this performative side of you?

130
00:13:42,947 --> 00:13:44,490
I'm not being performative.

131
00:13:45,199 --> 00:13:47,409
I'm adjusting too, just like you.

132
00:14:13,852 --> 00:14:17,439
It seems like you're being
a little too nice and cooperative, Chiara.

133
00:14:24,446 --> 00:14:26,073
You're being unfair to me, you know.

134
00:14:28,075 --> 00:14:30,911
When I'm confident and assertive,

135
00:14:30,995 --> 00:14:32,496
you think badly of me.

136
00:14:33,747 --> 00:14:36,709
And now that I'm making an effort
and trying to be nice,

137
00:14:36,792 --> 00:14:38,460
you still think badly of me.

138
00:14:39,503 --> 00:14:41,881
So where do I stand with you, Alex?

139
00:14:44,466 --> 00:14:46,010
I don't know, Chiara.

140
00:14:46,927 --> 00:14:48,512
But between the two of us,

141
00:14:49,013 --> 00:14:50,556
you're the one with a game plan.

142
00:14:52,558 --> 00:14:54,310
Whatever it is,

143
00:14:54,977 --> 00:14:56,145
stop it.

144
00:15:06,989 --> 00:15:08,699
Try being genuine.

145
00:15:09,533 --> 00:15:10,743
Because right now,

146
00:15:11,660 --> 00:15:13,037
you're fake.

147
00:15:13,746 --> 00:15:15,080
Like you're putting on a show.

148
00:15:16,957 --> 00:15:19,960
Careful. You might get evicted.

149
00:15:28,677 --> 00:15:32,640
Whatever you think about me,
you're wrong, Alex.

150
00:15:33,515 --> 00:15:34,433
I hope so.

151
00:15:36,101 --> 00:15:37,811
Because it'll be much worse if I'm right.

152
00:15:38,395 --> 00:15:39,563
Even worse

153
00:15:40,356 --> 00:15:43,275
if I never should've
trusted you in the first place.

154
00:15:48,280 --> 00:15:49,823
You know, I get it.

155
00:15:51,992 --> 00:15:53,410
Because honestly,

156
00:15:56,205 --> 00:15:58,415
And I know you're protective

157
00:15:58,499 --> 00:16:00,292
of everyone here.

158
00:16:01,043 --> 00:16:04,129
But I don't think you're doing this
just because it's your job.

159
00:16:12,638 --> 00:16:13,555
Wow.

160
00:16:34,326 --> 00:16:37,162
Too bad it looks like
you're starting to convince my boss.

161
00:16:47,089 --> 00:16:48,257
I don't know.

162
00:16:49,216 --> 00:16:52,678
General Norberto thinks
your proposal is worth considering.

163
00:16:53,637 --> 00:16:55,472
So he's going to accept my offer?

164
00:17:04,189 --> 00:17:08,152
The protocols and policies
of your dear agency.

165
00:17:09,653 --> 00:17:10,696
Don't worry.

166
00:17:11,280 --> 00:17:14,783
I'll let you know
if you successfully convince my boss.

167
00:17:33,594 --> 00:17:35,596
<i>Are you not hiding any more secrets?</i>

168
00:17:49,359 --> 00:17:50,194
So dedicated, huh.

169
00:17:51,695 --> 00:17:54,865
That'll make you stronger.
It'll toughen up your stomach.

170
00:17:58,869 --> 00:18:00,788
- Good morning, Agent Alex.
- Morning, ma'am.

171
00:18:05,751 --> 00:18:08,629
Now I know why Mikoy
is so in love with Chiara.

172
00:18:10,380 --> 00:18:11,715
Because she's fearless.

173
00:18:11,799 --> 00:18:15,219
She wasn't even intimidated
by the scary Agent Alex.

174
00:18:15,302 --> 00:18:16,136
That's true.

175
00:18:16,220 --> 00:18:19,014
As for me, I'm Team Alex.

176
00:18:19,098 --> 00:18:21,600
Look at you acting like
you're so close to her.

177
00:18:21,683 --> 00:18:23,102
On a different note.

178
00:18:23,185 --> 00:18:24,853
Here's a thought. What if…

179
00:18:25,354 --> 00:18:29,108
What if Mikoy had met Agent Alex first?

180
00:18:29,983 --> 00:18:31,693
Do you think they'd still end up together?

181
00:18:32,444 --> 00:18:33,904
Sure, they would.

182
00:18:34,446 --> 00:18:36,698
They'd make a great pair.
Both handsome and beautiful.

183
00:18:38,992 --> 00:18:40,744
- You guys, I swear.
- Hey, Mikoy!

184
00:18:40,828 --> 00:18:43,080
No matter where you end up,

185
00:18:43,163 --> 00:18:45,332
you still love gossiping
about other people's lives?

186
00:18:45,415 --> 00:18:46,875
It's too early for that!

187
00:18:46,959 --> 00:18:48,877
I bet you haven't even brushed
your teeth yet.

188
00:18:48,961 --> 00:18:51,004
Come on, Mikoy.

189
00:18:52,297 --> 00:18:54,925
On a different note,
I've got a serious question.

190
00:18:55,008 --> 00:18:57,261
From what I know about you,

191
00:18:57,761 --> 00:19:00,597
you're just a simple guy
who wants a simple life.

192
00:19:00,681 --> 00:19:04,768
So why did you date
a mafia boss's daughter?

193
00:19:04,852 --> 00:19:05,978
A boss, no less!

194
00:19:08,480 --> 00:19:09,606
I don't know.

195
00:19:10,899 --> 00:19:12,651
I guess that's what fate
had in store for me.

196
00:19:12,734 --> 00:19:16,029
Come on. People make their own fate.

197
00:19:16,697 --> 00:19:19,992
That's right. We may not have control
over everything,

198
00:19:20,075 --> 00:19:21,451
but we always have a choice.

199
00:19:22,411 --> 00:19:23,453
Look at you!

200
00:19:23,537 --> 00:19:25,539
Is this what happens
when you stop drinking?

201
00:19:25,622 --> 00:19:28,292
You're suddenly full of quotable quotes.

202
00:19:28,375 --> 00:19:31,044
Of course, we're motivated.

203
00:19:31,128 --> 00:19:32,504
After everything that's happened,

204
00:19:32,588 --> 00:19:35,883
we've started asking ourselves
a lot of "what ifs".

205
00:19:35,966 --> 00:19:37,634
Some pleasing scenarios.

206
00:19:38,135 --> 00:19:39,219
You know.

207
00:19:39,303 --> 00:19:42,306
Besides, buddy,
we're just concerned about you.

208
00:19:42,890 --> 00:19:44,641
Thanks for your concern.

209
00:19:44,725 --> 00:19:48,353
But instead of wasting our time
on "what ifs",

210
00:19:48,437 --> 00:19:51,648
let's focus on what is.

211
00:19:53,317 --> 00:19:55,652
"What if" isn't so bad either.

212
00:20:13,212 --> 00:20:17,174
For today's activity,
I want you to draw and color

213
00:20:17,257 --> 00:20:21,595
how you imagine Sitio San Juan
20 years from now.

214
00:20:21,678 --> 00:20:23,013
Sounds good?

215
00:20:23,096 --> 00:20:24,014
Mak-mak.

216
00:20:25,390 --> 00:20:27,017
So, Sofie,

217
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:31,647
20 years from now, I'll be as tall as you,

218
00:20:31,730 --> 00:20:33,190
so can I court you then?

219
00:20:34,107 --> 00:20:36,068
Oh, Mak-mak!

220
00:20:36,151 --> 00:20:37,319
Still no,

221
00:20:37,402 --> 00:20:41,198
because 20 years from now,
I'll probably have a husband and kids.

222
00:20:41,782 --> 00:20:42,741
What a shame!

223
00:20:43,408 --> 00:20:46,286
Who do you want to be with in the future?

224
00:20:47,079 --> 00:20:48,372
In the future?

225
00:20:53,627 --> 00:20:57,130
Someone who's like my best friend,
someone I can tell anything to.

226
00:20:57,214 --> 00:20:59,716
Even when we're married and have kids,

227
00:20:59,800 --> 00:21:02,094
our friendship will still be the same.

228
00:21:02,886 --> 00:21:04,263
So…

229
00:21:04,346 --> 00:21:06,556
can we still be friends?

230
00:21:07,808 --> 00:21:09,101
Of course!

231
00:21:09,184 --> 00:21:11,395
If you still remember me.

232
00:21:11,478 --> 00:21:14,439
Sounds like you don't want to.

233
00:21:14,523 --> 00:21:18,068
Sofie, what about my future?

234
00:21:19,736 --> 00:21:22,447
Oh, Mak-mak. You're still so young.

235
00:21:23,782 --> 00:21:26,702
You know, your future
is still going to be bright.

236
00:21:26,785 --> 00:21:28,912
Because you got to meet

237
00:21:28,996 --> 00:21:32,040
the beautiful, smart,

238
00:21:32,124 --> 00:21:33,875
and kind Sofie.

239
00:21:35,210 --> 00:21:36,545
Right?

240
00:21:37,546 --> 00:21:39,006
If it's a full house, you pay double!

241
00:21:43,176 --> 00:21:45,512
What a delicious breakfast, sweetheart!

242
00:21:45,595 --> 00:21:47,639
We have breakfast!

243
00:21:47,723 --> 00:21:48,849
- Wow!
- Awesome!

244
00:21:48,932 --> 00:21:54,146
Of course! Breakfast
is the most important meal of the day.

245
00:21:54,229 --> 00:21:55,939
- Exactly.
- Wait a second.

246
00:21:56,023 --> 00:21:57,816
It feels like something's missing.

247
00:21:58,483 --> 00:22:00,277
You're right! Hot sauce.

248
00:22:00,360 --> 00:22:01,403
And lots of calamansi.

249
00:22:01,486 --> 00:22:03,238
And coffee creamer!

250
00:22:03,322 --> 00:22:04,740
Okay, got it.

251
00:22:04,823 --> 00:22:05,657
- Anything else?
- No, wait!

252
00:22:05,741 --> 00:22:09,161
No, dear. That's not what I meant.
We're missing someone.

253
00:22:09,911 --> 00:22:10,871
Cocoy isn't here!

254
00:22:11,496 --> 00:22:12,372
- You're right!
- Yes.

255
00:22:12,456 --> 00:22:13,665
Huh?

256
00:22:13,749 --> 00:22:15,167
Cocoy is missing?

257
00:22:26,762 --> 00:22:27,804
Where's Cocoy?

258
00:22:29,473 --> 00:22:30,891
He's taking care of something.

259
00:22:30,974 --> 00:22:32,517
Doing what?

260
00:23:25,821 --> 00:23:26,863
Again, where is he, Chiara?

261
00:24:11,074 --> 00:24:13,034
La Fornarina.

262
00:24:16,246 --> 00:24:18,832
<i>Looks like Cocoy left the country.</i>

263
00:24:18,915 --> 00:24:21,501
Dara, tell me that Sir Norberto
didn’t know about this yet.

264
00:24:21,585 --> 00:24:22,252
Not yet.

265
00:24:22,335 --> 00:24:24,671
Please, don’t let him know yet.

266
00:24:24,754 --> 00:24:27,424
What is it that General
should not know and hear about?

267
00:24:28,383 --> 00:24:30,093
